Marvel's newest round of infinity war  toys have once again revealed perhaps a  bit too much about an upcoming movie in  the Marvel Cinematic Universe in case  you don't remember thor ragnarok saw the  Odinson lose his right eye in a battle  with his villainous sister hella the  goddess of death while losing an eye  barely inconvenienced the god of thunder  in combat it did mangle his look leaving  the hero bruised and battered and shorn  of his locks by the end of Ragnarok  where infinity war picks up Hasbro's  assortment of infinity war toys as well  as Funko's bobbleheads have made it  perfectly clear that thor doesn't lose  his eye permanently in fact he seems to  get it back in time for whatever big  battle the Avengers have against Thanos  but a few toys tell a slightly larger  story Paz bros Marvel Legends 3-pack  gives us a Thor with an eyepatch hanging  out with rocket and a teenaged Groot a  trio that's repeated in the Lego set and  hot toys teaser photos for their own  infinity war action figures a later wave  of Marvel Legends includes a second Thor  this time with two working eyes and a  fancy new axe with a handle made of  Groot  new cos baby figures from Hot Toys also  appear to show the full evolution and  Thor status quo fixing a setback the  character suffered in his most recent  solo movie if they do indeed reflect the  events of infinity war the two Thor  figures seem to tell a story of personal  growth and triumph for the mythical  Asgardian fighter the first figure shows  Thor with an eyepatch charging himself  up for combat Dragonball Z style he  still sports the scars of his battle  with hella with only one lightning  charge died visible all is as expected  the second figure introduces a two-eyed  Thor with new armor and a new weapon  scarring around the figures right eye is  consistent with the damage hella cost  with one big difference the eyeball is  back suggesting that the god of thunder  is going to regenerate his eye as a part  of the push against Thanos while  audiences have seen Thor spontaneously  generate magical armor around his body  before we've never seen him regrow an  actual body part if all of this turns  out to be true it begs the question why  hasn't Miri grown as  err life is about it's about growth it's  about change previously a toy called the  Hulk out Hulkbuster seemed to confirm a  major moment from the upcoming superhero  movie revealing that Bruce Banner will  wear one of Tony Stark's Hulkbuster Iron  Man suits before going green inside it  bursting out of the armor like a  vengeful angry nesting doll Wow however  it's worth noting that these tie-in  products aren't always on the money with  occasional liberties being taken with  the story for the sake of making a  kick-ass toy previous reports that a  lego set had revealed Thor to be using  the comic book weapon yarn Bjorn an  infinity war turned out to be not quite  accurate it was later confirmed that  Thor's weapon in the movie would be an  axe called Stormbreaker so as fun as it  is and as accurate as it might end up  being it's still worth taking all of  this toy sourced information with a  hefty abundance of salt we'll be able to  see for ourselves what happens to Thor  in adventures infinity war when the  movie launches in theaters worldwide on  April 27th thanks for watching click the  looper icon to subscribe to our YouTube  channel let's check out all this cool  stuff we know you love to  [Music]
 

